From b55fd2a9831bd5faf5e4078eeb4375c1e6c7776f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:28:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] sycl: keep graphs on for lazily reordered MUL_MAT and
 reject BN=64 combos on the device MoE schedule

The graph check disabled SYCL graphs until every MUL_MAT weight with a
reorder extra was reordered, which never happens for some (dense MXFP4,
the fused GLU plain path), so graphs stayed off and the check reran on
every compute. Upstream already reorders those during recording with
the async memory extension, so only MUL_MAT_ID weights are reordered
ahead of recording now.

ggml_sycl_grouped_dequant_gemm_device_supported() accepted any XMX
combo, but the device schedule only runs with BN == GGML_SYCL_FG_BN, so
a 32x64 combo (GGML_SYCL_XMX_GATHER_SHAPES=4 or 8) made the graph check
pass and the compute fall back to the host sync path while recording.

