Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:11:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix: stop erroneously reordering host-offloaded tensors

With -ncmoe, prompt processing offloads the CPU-resident expert matmuls
to the GPU: the scheduler uploads the experts into a copy in the compute
buffer before every run. init_tensor gave that copy a reorder record, so
the MUL_MAT_ID gather path reordered every offloaded expert tensor on
every ubatch, and the next upload overwrote the result.

Qwen3-30B-A3B Q4_K_M, 1x B60, llama-perplexity -c 4096 -ub 2048
-ncmoe 48, 8 chunks, on master ac8e1694:
  master                        116 s, PPL 7.739
  master XMX_GATHER_TYPES=0      67 s, PPL 7.738
  with this change               67 s, PPL 7.729

Refs ggml-org/llama.cpp#31262

